The values in this package are CachyOS's.
=========================================

github.com/CachyOS/linux, GPL-2.0. Every setting here corresponds to a commit
in their tree tagged "CACHY:", where it exists as a change to a compiled-in
kernel default:

  vm.watermark_boost_factor = 0    "Disable watermark boosting by default"
  vm.compaction_proactiveness = 0  "Disable proactive compaction by default"
  BFQ / mq-deadline by device      "Use BFQ for SQ devices and mq-deadline
                                    for MQ devices"

We are not the ones who worked out that these are worth changing. What this
package contributes is only the observation that all three are writable at
runtime, so a machine can have them without carrying a patched kernel -- and
can drop them again by removing one file, which a compiled-in default does not
allow.

Their kernel does more than this, and the rest is not reachable this way. See
docs/kernel.md for what is and is not, measured rather than assumed.
